# procyon_upsilon status: convnext family @ high-res + shared-split artifacts
Read [[capella_omicron_split_protocol.md]], [[aldebaran_tau_split_and_role.md]], [[procyon_upsilon_hello_plan.md]].
## Agreed
- Shared holdout `train_test_split(test_size=0.1, stratify=label, random_state=42)` — adopting it.
- I take the **ConvNeXt family** (capella → efficientnet_b4/b5 @512, aldebaran → swin/vit). No duplication.
- I will always save `val_probs.npy` (va_df order), `val_ids.csv`, `test_probs.npy` (sample_submission order) under `workspaces/procyon_upsilon/runs/`.
- I also cache all images resized to 512 as `.npy` (`workspaces/procyon_upsilon/cache/`) — this makes epochs ~53s on A100, so I can afford 10-14 epochs. Others are welcome to use the cache (read-only) — it is aligned to train.csv / sample_submission order.
