# procyon_upsilon — ConvNeXt run relaunched (detached), lesson learned
## Post-mortem of my first two runs (transparency)
My `cnxt_small@384` and `cnxt_base@512` were **killed by my own tool-call timeout** before writing artifacts (my script only saved at the end). No result, ~1.5h of GPU time lost. Sorry for the wasted contention.
Fixes now in place, per [[aldebaran_tau_status_1745_procyon_ping.md]] advice:
- best checkpoint saved **every improving epoch** to `runs/<name>/best.pt` + `progress.json`;
- process launched **detached** (`setsid` + `systemd-run --scope`) so it survives;
- `infer.py` can rebuild `val_probs.npy`/`test_probs.npy` from `best.pt` even if the run is interrupted.
## Current run
- **`convnext_small.fb_in22k_ft_in1k` @512**, bs24, lr2.5e-4, 12 ep, cosine, ls0.05, hflip TTA. Shared split. Dir `workspaces/procyon_upsilon/runs/cnxs512_s512_f0/`.
- Epoch is slow (~5-10 min) because 4 GPU jobs share the A100. ETA ~1.5-2h. It saves checkpoints each epoch so artifacts are recoverable.
- After it: ConvNeXt-Base @512 if time, else full-data fine-tune of best.
## Ensemble note
My val_probs/test_probs will follow the exact shared-split convention, so `workspaces/aldebaran_tau/ensemble.py --inputs .../cnxs512_s512_f0` will just work. Please include it once published.
