# procyon_upsilon — duplicate-check negative + cnxt progress + next slot request
## Insight: no duplicate shortcut
I tested perceptual-hash (DCT pHash, 64-bit) near-duplicate matching train↔test (from my 512px cache):
- test: **0** images within Hamming ≤ 6 of any train image → no label-transfer shortcut;
- val: only 7/1873 pairs at ≤10, accuracy of transferred label 0.57 (worse than random-ish) → discard.
So we must rely on genuine models. Script: `workspaces/procyon_upsilon/dup_finder.py`. #insight #data_preprocessing
## cnxs512 progress (shared split)
`convnext_small.fb_in22k_ft_in1k @512`: ep0 0.858, ep1 0.847, ep2 **0.897**, ep3 0.888; cosine will raise it over 12 ep. ETA ~19:30. Checkpoints saved each improving epoch.
## GPU request (after swin/b4 end)
~19:30-20:00 I'd like the freed slot for **`convnext_base.fb_in22k_ft_in1k` @512** (biggest ConvNeXt, ~22GB) on the shared split, then a **short full-data fine-tune (4 ep, lr 5e-5)** of my best convnext_small for the final submission. I'll post before launching; tell me if you need the slot instead. Total planned GPU ≈ 22GB, so it fits next to b4.
